  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 134 AM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nA passing shortwave this weekend will bring periods of showers\nwith slight chances for thunderstorms with 50-70% PoPs. The\nhighest chances for rain are late Saturday into Saturday night.\nNBM probabilities for >0.50\" of rain through the weekend is\n20-50% north of I-44 and <20% south of I-44, so rainfall amounts\nare expected to be light.\n\nUncertainty increases into the middle of next week as models\ngenerally show a deep trough moving through the central CONUS,\nwith the average timing of greatest precip among model guidance\nbeing late Tuesday into early Wednesday at 60-70%. Depending \non details that can't be resolved yet, or are below a reasonable\nlevel of confidence, there could be a severe weather threat \ngiven the general setup. AI/ML severe weather probabilities do \nhighlight the time frame for a low end risk, so will continue \nmonitoring and updating as necessary. NMB rainfall probabilites\nare 60-70% of >= 1\", 40-50% of >= 2\", and 20-30% chance for >=\n3\".",
